okay so with my academia and black  clover both entering their final arcs  it's no surprise that the authors have  been trying to wrap up several lingering  plot lines for example in the past 18  months of my hero we've witnessed  dabby's backstory deco unlocking nearly  all of his quirks and most recently the  reveal of the ua traitor this is a  storyline that was set into motion so  long ago that after a while there were  people online who genuinely believed the  harakos had forgotten about it with that  much time to plan things out you'd  expect the eventual traitor revealed to  be an iconic moment for the series on  par with other famous events but  unfortunately that's not what ended up  happening instead what we got was an  okay reveal that was lacking in a few  different ways and for me personally i  didn't realize just how underwhelming it  was until black clover recently swooped  in with a traitor reveal of its own in  this video i'll be explaining why as a  fan of both series black clover did  everything right when it came to  exposing who the traitor is while on  this occasion my hero didn't have the  same impact  before we get into it don't forget to  hit that sub button for more anime and  manga content like this and as the video  continues feel free to let me know  whether you agree or disagree in the  comments down below  okay so for those of you watching who  have no idea what happened in either  series i'm gonna do a very quick recap  but obviously there will be massive  spoilers ahead in my here academia the  uh traitor was revealed to be aoyama  after his parents were caught loudly  talking about it in the forest if they'd  been whispering instead then it's  possible they never would have been  found out but in this case higgakurei  overheard their conversation soon  afterwards the family were arrested but  within just two chapters it was decided  that aoyama wouldn't be expelled and his  classmates had all chosen to forgive him  the reason for this was that although he  betrayed them he only did these things  because all for one was threatening his  family by contrast to this in black  clover the trait was revealed to be the  wizard king julius who turned out to be  the mastermind behind the dark triad the  dark triad have essentially been the  main villains of this manga for the last  couple years but in reality julius is  their older brother and his real name is  lucia segratus this twist was easily one  of the most surprising moments of the  entire series and it was so well  executed that even though i predicted it  might happen six months earlier the  reveal still caught me completely off  guard in order to explain why that is  we're about to examine the four key  elements that make an effective trait to  reveal in my opinion the first of those  elements being trust it sounds obvious  to say this but the more we trust a  character and believe they're a good  person the more shocking it is if they  turn out to not be who we think this is  because trustworthy characters have  repeatedly done things said things and  thought things that have convinced us of  who they are so much so that it's hard  to imagine they could be anything else  purely as an example todoroki and yuno  are two characters who have earned the  complete trust of the audience to the  point where even if there was a hint  that they might secretly be evil most  people wouldn't take it seriously  instead what we'd likely do is wait for  there to be more concrete evidence since  either of them being traitors wouldn't  fit in with everything we know  this same logic applies to julius  because although there were a few sus  things about him that we'll be talking  about later for the most part he had  earned our trust  thanks to his internal monologues he'd  proven consistently that his main goal  was to end discrimination in the clover  kingdom and to achieve that mission he  often showed kindness to people who were  outcast by society whereas most nobles  only cared about their own social class  and their own wealth julius was the one  who had faith in the potential of all  humans regardless of whether they  happened to be a peasant as wizard king  he then took steps that led to his dream  becoming more of a reality and when it  came down to it he was willing to die to  ensure the progress they made wasn't  lost  everything considered the wizard king is  a character who gained the trust of the  audience and judging from chat to 331  julius himself didn't know he was the  traitor  rather his character seems to be a porn  of lucius in a comparable way to how  aoyama is appointable for one but the  key difference here is that julius is  someone we trusted  when it comes to aoyama for the first  300 chapters we rarely ever heard what  he was thinking and his behavior was  easily the most suspected class 1a if  you would ask any myhera fan who among  classes was most likely to be the  traitor the usual answer was either him  or invisible girl because we didn't know  anything about them and they gave us no  real reason to trust them aoyama in  particular was described by deku as a  loner who doesn't go out of his way to  make friends and unlike the main  characters his motivations in life were  also unclear in spite of being on the  hero course his conviction was lacking  compared to the other kids partly  demonstrated by how easily he was  prepared to give up during the hero  license exam  of course that's not to say that he's  not been heroic at all because more  often than not he does eventually do the  right thing but the point i'm making is  that until recently we never saw inside  his head and therefore never knew what  was driving him this is a large factor  in why it was so easy to believe that he  could be the traitor and so when it  turned out to be him the only surprising  thing about it was that it wasn't  hagakurei for that reason black clover  wins when it comes to building trust  which ultimately made this moment a lot  more exciting  now moving on for a traitor revealed to  be truly mind-blowing it can't be too  predictable but at the same time it also  can't just come out of nowhere with  nothing to back it up that's why an  effective reveal benefits from setup  which in this context means small clues  throughout the story that subtly  indicate who a person really is  in my opinion neither series did a bad  job of this although my hero loses out  again because there were times when the  hints just became way too obvious  examples of this include the usg attack  where ayama went missing the entire time  and then breaks the fourth wall to tell  us his location was a secret on top of  that there was the episode when he was  acting super weird towards deku and the  narration even said that this was when  ayama began showing his true self stuff  like this contributed to why the reveal  felt so unsurprising but that doesn't  mean there weren't other hints that were  more subtle for instance his  incompatibility with his quirk was a  running theme since he was first  introduced and it was comparable to how  midoriya himself was struggling with one  for all this parallel was clever  foreshadowing of how they both received  the power derived from all for one and  it's one of the many clues that prove  herokuchi planned for him to be the  traitor from the beginning a different  hint that only made sense after the  reveal happened was aoyama's reaction to  all might fighting afo although we  didn't know it the reason they were  emotional was because they thought this  might be their chance to finally be free  of off one's influence in that sense the  setup for his reveal was mostly good  like i said but certain aspects were way  too obvious which contributed to its  predictability compared to this black  clover handled things more discreetly  with the setup consisting only of small  things that didn't cause too much  suspicion by themselves starting from  the beginning the first time we properly  meet julius is in chapter 10 when he was  sneaking around the clover kingdom  looking for new types of magic in this  moment he takes a strong fascination  with asta's abilities and in hindsight  this was our first clue as we now know  lucius needed three things for his plan  to succeed number one was someone with  dark magic number two was someone with  world tree magic and number three was  someone with the power to defeat  lucifero having already acquired yarmy  and william astor was the final piece of  the puzzle hence how lucius was so sure  that things would be going his way  the next hint came when their main  characters met the wizard king as he was  able to recognize the devil language in  astu's gramoire based on what we know of  lucius everything points to him being  the most talented person when it comes  to devil possession and later in the  series julius is shown to share at least  some of that extensive devil knowledge  despite that though in this scene he  pretends to not know anything about it  and looking back now that is incredibly  suspicious  another clue that makes more sense in  the present day is julius's actions in  the fight against party during that  fight the wizard king refused to use any  lethal force since killing parchee would  have also meant that william would be  killed as well at the time he believed  this was because he cared about william  and to an extent that might still be  true however we can't deny that lucius  had an influence since he needed  williams magic to open the gate to the  underworld  without world tree magic lucius's entire  plan would have fallen apart so the  wizard king's reluctance to kill vandals  now has a whole new context  anyhow there were a bunch of other small  hints exactly like the ones i've just  mentioned including how the shadow  palace has the same symbol as the one in  lucius's head in that way there was a  ton of setup for julius being the  traitor but nothing so obvious that  you'd be certain it would happen  switching over to the execution this  element is all about how the reveal  actually went down for mario academia  everything begins with all for one in  chapter 335 afo was bragging about how  he has multiple ways to achieve a single  ambition and during this speech he was  confirmed that he has a mole inside ua  harakoshi ended that chapter by heavily  implying that the mall was invisible  girl mainly because he knew we'd believe  it for the reasons i mentioned earlier  that being said in the next chapter the  traitor was confirmed to be the other  most suspicious classmate and in terms  of execution there was a big problem  given that this storyline was set up so  many years ago it was disappointing for  the trailer only to be exposed because  the ariamas were too clueless to use  their inside voices to me it felt like  hurricane was looking for a way to  swiftly wrap up this plot thread and  yuga's parents accidentally revealing  everything to hagakure well that was a  quick way of doing that  in the end it just seemed way too  convenient which is a shame because i  did actually like the backstory about  how aliama received the quirk from afo  in the case of black clover's execution  the betrayal happens in chapter 331  with a concerned looking damnatio  walking through the royal capital at  this time we had no idea what was about  to come because up until this point no  one had even mentioned the idea of there  being a traitor the scene then switches  over to the wizard king who's receiving  an update about how asta and the magic  knights have defeated the dark triad  julius then responds to this news with  genuine relief and it's clear from his  inner monologue that he is on the side  of the clover kingdom however he then  goes on to think that something doesn't  feel quite right and this is when  damnatio enters the room  over the next couple pages damnatio  explains that he's been researching the  existence of devils and according to the  records a devil known as asteroth  vanished from the underworld more than  20 years ago asteroth was one of the  three most powerful devils in existence  and just like julius his magic attribute  was time magic  as this info is being revealed we hear  damnatio's in a monologue in which he  desperately hopes there's no connection  between the supreme devil and the wizard  king as the page then turns julius comes  to the realization that he is asteroth  and his expression indicates that he's  only just now understanding what he  really is i thought this moment was  especially interesting because in the  past he has mentioned how he always used  to ask himself this question  over the following seconds he  frantically gives damnatio a warning but  is interrupted as his body  uncontrollably starts to transform then  for the first time ever his previously  coverless grimoire generates a cover out  of nowhere revealing that the clover  kingdom's wizard king has actually been  from the spay kingdom this entire time  that info by itself would have been a  cliffhanger worthy of ending any chapter  but as things continue we get the  additional reveal that julius is now a  completely different person  overall the execution of this was well  written with tabata starting off by  luring us into a false sense of security  as he reinforced the idea that julius is  on the right side this loyalty is then  reluctantly brought into question by  damnatio but before we have any time to  form a real conclusion the wizard king  himself straight up confirms that he's a  devil what follows this is three pages  of unexpected hype that any black clover  fan would appreciate and by the end of  it it seems like everything happened  exactly the way lucius intended  finally this brings us to the fourth  element of a good trait to reveal which  is the impact it has on other characters  and the world itself  as the wizard king julius being a devil  host has huge political ramifications  hence why this final arc is called the  ultimate wizard king what this title  suggests is that when all is said and  done someone will need to replace him in  that position and depending on who the  next person is it could permanently  change the social dynamics of the  kingdom furthermore lucius's grand plan  to remake humanity will affect thousands  if not millions of people so his reveal  does have a significant impact on  virtually everyone  now moving down to a more personal level  as i'm making this video black clover is  currently on hiatus so we don't yet know  how characters like yarmy and william  will react with julius being their  mentor they're understandably going to  be devastated to find out who he really  is while astor and yuna will also likely  find it hard to accept however right now  that is just speculation until the  series comes back so all we can be sure  of is that lucius will have a huge  impact on the world because he pretty  much said it but in terms of the  individual impact we just can't know  when it comes to my cure academia  aliama's betrayal has already had  different kinds of impacts one of which  is the impact on class 1a up till now  they've been put through all sorts of  hell because of the traitor including  froppy being an inch away from death  bakago being kidnapped by the villains  all might losing one for all and deku  genuinely thinking he was about to die  against muscular these were some of the  most traumatic moments of their lives  caused by aoyama's actions so it was a  bit jarring that everyone was ready to  move on so quickly without any  significant debate for a bit of context  alyama was arrested halfway through  chapter 337 and before we even got to  halfway through the next chapter the  students had decided to move on  if there had been a longer more  meaningful discussion between the class  then i think forgiving him would have  been fine but the way it happened made  it seem like the impact of his betrayal  wasn't really a big factor  that being said on the other side  something that was done better was the  impact the ioma's reveal had on the  villains by his secret being exposed it  gave the heroes a chance to form a new  plan to take down all for one with yuga  being used as debate to lure him out  luckily this plan did actually end up  working and seemingly for the first time  ever afo himself had actually been  tricked based on that the traitor  storyline will have a big impact on how  the final arc plays out and even though  aoyama might not face harsh consequences  from the heroes recent chapters make it  seem like he might face retribution from  the villains overall with black clover  being on hiatus it's not fair for me to  say which of these reveals will have the  longer term impact but based on the  positives and negatives that we've just  heard about mha let me know in the  comments how you think black clover will  do by comparison  before we end the video one side note i  wanted to mention is that harukoshi  recently confirmed that his original  plan was to expose aoyama during the  forest training camp although we'll  likely never know how the original  reveal was supposed to happen at the  very least it wouldn't have involved  ayama's parents just blurting it out  which is good enough  anyway don't forget to sub to the  channel if you haven't already and as  always drop a like if you like the video  until the next one peace out

